<https://teater.aiscr.cz/id/1264> rdf:type skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://teater.aiscr.cz/id/1257> ;
    skos:broaderTransitive <https://teater.aiscr.cz/id/1050> ;
    skos:broaderTransitive <https://teater.aiscr.cz/id/1070> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/atrium/scheme/teater-harvest> ;
    skos:notation "1264" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Frühe Neuzeit (e)"@de ;
    skos:prefLabel "early modern period"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "raný novověk"@cs ;
    skos:scopeNote "The ‘early modern period’ is defined as a transitional age when the structures of the medieval way of life were still alive, whereas at the same time developments were on their way which would lead to the present state of things. However, old and new cannot be separated neatly. On the contrary, it is exactly their mutual interpenetration which characterizes the ‘early modern period’ (‘Frühe Neuzeit’) as that part of our modern age (‘Neuzeit’) which still disavowed its modernity (ibid. 365). Norms and legitimation were grounded on the idea of a stable world and therefore claimed permanent validity. Innovations were rarely accepted; to prove innovation meant to discredit a case. Special strategies had to be developed to master that change which had become unavoidable. They all resemble each other, because they always try to fit things into an immutable order."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "počátek se datuje do roku 1453 (dobytí Konstantinopole), 1492 (dobytí Granady, objevení Ameriky), 1517 (Luterovy teze), 1526 (používáné v českém prostředí, smrt Ludvíka Jagellonského a nástup Ferdinanda I.), konec do roku 1789 (Velká francouzská revoluce)"@cs .

